			<div class="content" id="post-content-2239330">
									

<p>In a scientific/engineering sense, &quot;metastable&quot; does <em>NOT</em> mean &quot;super-stable&quot;. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">It means that the whatever is currently stable, but very very easy to destabilize. For instance, if you managed to balance a sharpened pencil on its tip, it'd be metastable: perferctly fine and balanced <em>so long as absolutely nothing touches it</em>.</span><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-788425-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-788425-1')">1</a></sup> In this case, ice XII is metastable in that it <em>normally</em> only forms at very specific heat/temperature combinations and outside of that it turns into a different form of ice/water. SCP-045 is able to remain in the form of ice XII within a <em>massively</em> increased range, which is part of its anomalous properties.</p>
